The quotation is centrally about extending government-funded childcare to disadvantaged families who are caught in a poverty/work trap — supporting parents into work and children's early development. This is about welfare provision and its effects on poverty and work, fitting I38 (Government Policy • Provision and Effects of Welfare Programs).

While there's an education/early years dimension, the core mechanism described is breaking a poverty trap through welfare program extension, not education policy per se.

